        <body>
            <div xml:id="d97">

                <pb facs="0102" n="96" sameAs="frus:frus1894app1/pg96"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Sill to Mr.
                            Gresham.</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 98.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Seoul, Korea</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1895-01-18"><hi rendition="#italic">January 18, 1895</hi></date>.
                        (Received February 19.)</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to my dispatch of yesterday’s
                    date, I now have the honor to send you a translation of the King’s order in
                    council, which order appeared in the Official Gazette of January 11. In this
                    order His <pb facs="0103" n="97" xml:id="pg97"/> Majesty begins to put into
                    force some of the reforms mentioned in the oath, a copy of which was inclosed in
                    the above dispatch of January 17.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">John M. B. Sill.</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d97-a1.xml" xpointer="d97-a1"/>
